  "stage": "post-810264c-private-causal-coverage",
  "question": "After the exact Ember-overflow to Heavy-Blow representation closes, does a finite causal-topology partition contain one remaining complete legal private counter, tag or transform contract, or is the fourth owner-ordered causal class now validly exhausted?",
  "hypotheses": {
    "H0": "Every source- and evidence-selected private causal topology is an immutable closure alias or the now-closed overflow representation; a genuinely new topology lacks the producer, consumer, payoff and activation semantics needed for scientific selection.",
    "H1": "Exactly one complete materially distinct twelve-field topology remains legal under the current authority and frozen lexicographic objective."
  },
  "claimBoundary": "Exact-source and immutable-decision causal-topology coverage, twelve-field completeness, method decision value and authority trigger only. No support, simulator, causal endpoint, balance, product, protected-seed, acceptance or P9 claim.",
  "scientificBasis": {
    "correction": "Storage carrier and causal topology are different objects. The archived six-carrier audit remains evidence but cannot establish producer-to-consumer exhaustion.",
    "partition": "A deterministic producer is either one current-main transition, a deterministic order/identity/arithmetic relation over current-main transitions, or a genuinely new semantic transition. Relation forms reduce to order/lifecycle, target/instance identity, or threshold/precision/excess/residual for the smallest one-mediator grammar. Selector or persistent commitment is separate because it changes the authority boundary.",
    "selectionGate": "Source compatibility means implementable on current source. Scientific selection additionally requires exact source or immutable evidence to select the producer, consumer, bounded payoff and activation objective. Canonical SHA may break a tie between complete contracts but cannot author missing fields.",
    "noGuessing": "No topology may pass by naming a card pair, event subset, threshold, payoff or lifecycle not selected before support. No support, cache, outcome, simulator, model, ML, RL or optimiser is read."
  },
